nodes:
  - id: source-1
    type: pipeline
    position:
      x: 100
      y: 150
    data:
      label: Create
      type: SOURCE
      iconName: Box
      beam_transform: Create
      properties:
        elements:
          - '{"timestamp": "2026-09-01T12:00:00Z", "session_id": "sess-01",
            "action": "page_view", "version": "1.0"}'
          - '{"timestamp": "2026-09-01T12:01:00Z", "session_id": "sess-02",
            "action": "purchase", "version": "1.0"}'
    width: 180
    height: 62
  - id: step-pardo-2
    type: pipeline
    position:
      x: 380
      y: 150
    data:
      label: Project To Columns And Batch
      type: STEP
      iconName: Code
      beam_transform: ParDo
      system_instructions: Parse each input JSON string into a dict projected onto the
        Tinybird Data Source columns timestamp, session_id, action, version,
        payload (payload = json.dumps of the original event), and group the
        projected dicts into lists using beam.BatchElements(min_batch_size=1,
        max_batch_size=1000) because tinybird-beam's WriteToTinybird requires
        every input element to be an iterable of dicts (a batch), never a single
        dict. Unit-test the projection logic with TestPipeline, beam.Create and
        assert_that/equal_to.
    width: 190
    height: 64
  - id: sink-3
    type: pipeline
    position:
      x: 660
      y: 150
    data:
      label: Tinybird
      type: SINK
      iconName: Database
      beam_transform: Tinybird
      properties:
        host: https://api.tinybird.co
        tokenSecret: tinybird-append-token
        datasource: web_events
        columns: timestamp,session_id,action,version,payload
        batchingMode: none
      system_instructions: "Ingest the batches with the official Tinybird connector:
        `from tinybird.beam import WriteToTinybird` (PyPI package
        `tinybird-beam`; add `tinybird-beam` and `google-cloud-secret-manager`
        to requirements.txt; do NOT write a custom requests/HTTP DoFn). Resolve
        tokenSecret ONCE at pipeline construction with token =
        _access_secret(project_id, 'tinybird-append-token') where project_id
        comes from the GoogleCloudOptions project option, then apply
        WriteToTinybird('https://api.tinybird.co', token, 'web_events',
        'timestamp,session_id,action,version,payload'.split(',')) positionally
        as (host, token, data_source, columns). Never log the token, never give
        it an argparse default or environment-variable fallback."
    width: 190
    height: 64
edges:
  - id: edge-source-1-to-step-pardo-2
    source: source-1
    target: step-pardo-2
  - id: edge-step-pardo-2-to-sink-3
    source: step-pardo-2
    target: sink-3
runtimeVariables:
  - key: ENVIRONMENT
    value: python
  - key: JOB_ID
    value: tinybird-sink-python
jobConfig:
  runner: DirectRunner
  machineType: n1-standard-2
  minInstances: 1
  maxInstances: 5
  gcsStagingPath: gs://my-bucket/staging/python
  network: ""
  subnetwork: ""
pipelineConfig:
  language: Python
  outputFolder: pipelines/python/tinybird-sink-python
  needsRebuild: false
